    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "conductor_length",
          "label": "Conductor Length",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 1000,
          "unit": "ft"
        },
        {
          "id": "resistance_per_1000ft",
          "label": "Resistance (per 1000 ft)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 0.0173,
          "unit": "ohm"
        },
        {
          "id": "current",
          "label": "Current",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 100,
          "unit": "A"
        },
        {
          "id": "weight_per_1000ft",
          "label": "Weight (per 1000 ft)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 937,
          "unit": "lb"
        },
        {
          "id": "breaking_strength",
          "label": "Breaking Strength (per conductor)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 0.0182,
          "unit": "lb"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "total_resistance",
          "label": "Total Resistance",
          "formula": "(inputs.conductor_length / 1000) * inputs.resistance_per_1000ft",
          "unit": "ohm",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "voltage_drop",
          "label": "Voltage Drop",
          "formula": "inputs.current * ((inputs.conductor_length / 1000) * inputs.resistance_per_1000ft)",
          "unit": "V",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "power_loss",
          "label": "Power Loss",
          "formula": "inputs.current * inputs.current * ((inputs.conductor_length / 1000) * inputs.resistance_per_1000ft)",
          "unit": "W",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "total_weight",
          "label": "Total Conductor Weight",
          "formula": "(inputs.conductor_length / 1000) * inputs.weight_per_1000ft",
          "unit": "lb",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "total_breaking_strength",
          "label": "Total Breaking Strength",
          "formula": "inputs.breaking_strength * 1000",
          "unit": "lb",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Aluminum Conductor Reference Information\n\n### Key Definitions\n\n**GMR (Geometric Mean Radius)** - Quantifies a conductor's internal inductance. By definition, the GMR is the radius of an infinitely thin tube having the same internal inductance as the conductor out to a one-foot radius. GMR is often expressed in feet to ease calculations with distances measured in feet. Note that the GMR is less than the actual conductor radius.\n\n**kcmil (Thousand Circular Mils)** - A unit of conductor cross-sectional area where:\n- 1 kcmil = 1000 cmil\n- 1 kcmil = 785.4×10⁻⁶ in²\n- 1 kcmil = 0.5067 mm²\n\n### Unit Conversions\n- 1 ft = 0.3048 m\n- Resistance values are referenced at 60 Hz AC at 25°C\n\n### AAC Advantages\n- Lightweight compared to copper\n- Lower cost than copper\n- Suitable for transmission and distribution lines\n- Available in multiple strand configurations for different breaking strength requirements"
    }
  ]
